OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30508
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1786162661
OL,3,CBluetongue virus rapidly spreading
OL,4,Camong sheep with heatwave to blame
OL,6,FThere are 183 cases of bluetongue in
OL,7,Fthe UK. This latest surge has been
OL,8,Flinked by the National Farmers Union
OL,9,F(NFU) to prolonged hot weather and
OL,10,Fdrought, which it says has led to
OL,11,Freduced food production and increased
OL,12,Fcosts for farmers.
OL,14,FRobyn Munt, NFU vice president, said:
OL,15,F"Bluetongue and this peak of infection
OL,16,Fis falling at the same time that
OL,17,Ffarmers are struggling with water and
OL,18,Fgetting forage to their animals.
OL,20,F"So the mental load on farmers at the
OL,21,Fmoment is really significant."
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
